      "message": "I can\u0027t tell - there\u0027s no real information on this problem that I can dig up. I did find the code for the vzeroupper pass in their open-source clang repo [1], and it already has logic to avoid prefixing things like _chkstk (according to the comments). It\u0027s possible that the actual fix came when they fixed the properties of chkstk_darwin at some point (so the vzeroupper pass knew to ignore it).  I also realized that we were only doing the workaround on debug builds, so we\u0027ve been relying on optimized functions having small enough stacks that the bug didn\u0027t trigger anyway.",
